## Build with the application

The documentation is part of the same Go application and deployment. There is no separate docs runtime to operate.

Run the normal checks before publishing:

```bash
go test ./...
```

## Check the production URLs

After deployment, verify one rendered page and its Markdown equivalent:

```bash
curl --fail https://example.com/docs
curl --fail https://example.com/docs.md
```

Add those URLs to the same uptime and link checks as the rest of the public site.
